-- title:
--   Theorem 6.1 (corrected sampling condition) — all-node and first-stage convergence of Algorithm 3
-- statement:
--   Consider the node-dependent dynamic programming equations (6.43)–(6.44) on an arbitrary finite scenario tree with $T\ge1$ stages, and the decisions and approximations generated by Algorithm 3 at every node. Assume all of (H2), positive conditional tree probabilities, coherent node risk measures in the dual representation, and independent samples of the entire finite scenario, with the tree's scenario law. The latter is the independent-sample reading in the introductory prose of Theorem 6.1, correcting its constant selected-leaf indicator notation.
--
--   Almost surely, for every node $n$ other than the fictitious root, including leaves,
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\bigl(\mathcal Q^k_n(x^k_{[n]})-\mathcal Q_n(x^k_{[n]})\bigr)=0.$$
--   Moreover, almost surely the approximate first-stage optimal values converge to the true first-stage optimum, and every accumulation point of the first-stage decisions is optimal for that first-stage problem. These are all clauses of Theorem 6.1. No restriction to sampled nodes or a subsequence replaces its all-node limit.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The independent-scenario correction excludes the repeated, correlated scenario process exhibited in the companion `theorem_6_1_counterexample`. That process has correct individual scenario laws and independent identically-one selected-leaf indicators, but fails the two value limits. The current theorem uses the stronger condition explicitly stated in the source prose. It retains every conclusion and all of (H2), without assuming (H1). Risk supremum attainment is part of the run choices, not a new closedness assumption. The startup convention treats feasible decisions as minimizers of the initial constant $-\infty$ objective.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: Theorem 6.1 defines independence using the selected-leaf indicators, which are identically one → whole scenario vectors are independent across iterations; reason: the preceding prose explicitly requires independent samples and the proof on p. 21 invokes the SLLN as in Theorem 4.1; the repeated-scenario counterexample shows that the printed indicator test alone is insufficient
--   - reading: sample a scenario for the finite process and use the transition probabilities Phi_m → measurable tree-consistent paths have the conditional law specified by the positive transition probabilities; reason: a finite path is determined by its leaf and ancestors, so these probabilities specify exactly the source scenario law, without imposing interstage independence
--   - generalization: on-path cut slopes obtained from the multipliers in (6.48) → any subgradient of the indicated child value function; reason: the paper explicitly calls (6.48) a subgradient; every printed selection is included
--   - correction: initial continuation is minus infinity although a finite epigraph minimizer need not exist → choose any feasible minimizer of the extended-real startup objective; reason: Algorithm 3 solves (6.45), whose extended-real objective and initialization determine this boundary convention
--   - encoding: finite scenario tree with full decision histories and node risk measures → arbitrary finite level types, parent maps, Euclidean histories, EReal values and deterministic choice rules; reason: these encode every finite source tree; no uniform branching or interstage independence assumption is added
-- source:
--   Guigues, arXiv:1408.4439v4, p. 20, Theorem 6.1 (corrected independent-scenario condition), Algorithm 3, pp. 19–20

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RiskAverseSDDP_Convergence_Basic
import Definitions.Def_RiskAverseSDDP_Subdiff_Supplement_TreeModel
import Definitions.Def_RiskAverseSDDP_Subdiff_Supplement_Algorithm3
open Filter Topology MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace RiskAverseSDDP.Subdiff.Supplement

open RiskAverseSDDP.Convergence

/-- Full Theorem 6.1, with independence of whole sampled scenarios as its introductory
prose requires, correcting its constant selected-leaf indicator notation. -/
theorem theorem_6_1 {T n q p : ℕ} {V : ℕ → Type*} [∀ s, Fintype (V s)]
    [∀ s, MeasurableSpace (V s)] [∀ s, MeasurableSingletonClass (V s)]
    (D : TreeModel T n q p V) (hT : 1 ≤ T) (hS : D.Standing) (ε : ℝ) (hH2 : D.H2 ε)
    (R : TreeRules D) {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (ξ : ℕ → Ω → D.Path) (hSample : D.Sampling hT P ξ)
    (r : Ω → TreeRunData n V) (hr : ∀ ω, D.IsRun3 R (fun k => ξ k ω) (r ω)) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂P,
      (∀ s, s < T → ∀ ν : V s,
        Tendsto (fun k => (r ω).Qm k s ν ((r ω).hist D k s ν) - D.Q s ν ((r ω).hist D k s ν))
          atTop (𝓝 0)) ∧
      Tendsto (fun k => D.stageVal 0 D.first ((r ω).Qm k 0 D.first) (Hist.empty n))
        atTop (𝓝 D.Q1) ∧
      (∀ y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n),
        MapClusterPt y atTop (fun k => (r ω).x k 0 D.first) → D.IsFirstStageOptimal y) := by sorry

end RiskAverseSDDP.Subdiff.Supplement
